.TH SDL_LoadFileAsync 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_LoadFileAsync \- Load all the data from a file path, asynchronously.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_asyncio.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_LoadFileAsync(const char *file, SDL_AsyncIOQueue *queue, void *userdata);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function returns as quickly as possible; it does not wait for the read to complete\[char46] On a successful return, this work will continue in the background\[char46] If the work begins, even failure is asynchronous: a failing return value from this function only means the work couldn\(aqt start at all\[char46]
.PP
The data is allocated with a zero byte at the end (null terminated) for convenience\[char46] This extra byte is not included in
.BR SDL_AsyncIOOutcome \(aqs
bytes_transferred value\[char46]
.PP
This function will allocate the buffer to contain the file\[char46] It must be deallocated by calling
.BR SDL_free ()
on
.BR SDL_AsyncIOOutcome \(aqs
buffer field after completion\[char46]
.PP
An
.BR SDL_AsyncIOQueue
must be specified\[char46] The newly-created task will be added to it when it completes its work\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I file
the path to read all available data from\[char46]
.TP
.I queue
a queue to add the new
.BR SDL_AsyncIO
to\[char46]
.TP
.I userdata
an app-defined pointer that will be provided with the task results\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_LoadFile_IO (3)
